TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB003",
  "title": "Alarm Handling",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "requirements": "# Alarm Handling\n\n- **Difficulty:** Easy (easy)\n\n## Requirements\n\nIn industrial automation systems, monitoring the status of equipment is crucial. When equipment parameters exceed the normal range, the system needs to issue an alarm. To avoid frequent triggering of alarms due to minor fluctuations in parameters, an alarm management system with hysteresis function needs to be implemented.\nWhen Value is greater than hiLevel, trigger high alarm hiAlarm.\nWhen Value is less than hiLevel-hystWindow, exit high alarm hiAlarm.\nWhen Value is less than loLevel, trigger low alarm loAlarm.\nWhen Value is greater than loLevel+hystWindow, exit low alarm loAlarm.\nIf loLevel is greater than or equal to hiLevel, output error error=true, status=16#8001, and exit the program\nIf the hysteresis window value hystWindow is greater than or equal to the deviation range between hiLevel and loLevel, output error error=true, status=16#8002\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `Value` | `REAL` | Input value |\n| Input | `hiLevel` | `REAL` | High limit alarm value |\n| Input | `loLevel` | `REAL` | Low limit alarm value |\n| Input | `hystWindow` | `REAL` | Hysteresis window |\n| Output | `hiAlarm` | `BOOL` | High limit alarm |\n| Output | `loAlarm` | `BOOL` | Low limit alarm |\n| Output | `error` | `BOOL` | FALSE: No error occurred;<br>TRUE: Error occurred during execution of FB |\n| Output | `status` | `WORD` | Status code |",
  "scenario": "In industrial automation systems, monitoring the status of equipment is crucial. When equipment parameters exceed the normal range, the system needs to issue an alarm. To avoid frequent triggering of alarms due to minor fluctuations in parameters, an alarm management system with hysteresis function needs to be implemented.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "Value",
      "type": "REAL",
      "description": "Input value"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "hiLevel",
      "type": "REAL",
      "description": "High limit alarm value"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "loLevel",
      "type": "REAL",
      "description": "Low limit alarm value"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "hystWindow",
      "type": "REAL",
      "description": "Hysteresis window"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "hiAlarm",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "High limit alarm"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "loAlarm",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Low limit alarm"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "error",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "FALSE: No error occurred;<br>TRUE: Error occurred during execution of FB"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "status",
      "type": "WORD",
      "description": "Status code"
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "hiAlarm": false,
    "loAlarm": false,
    "error": false,
    "status": 0
  },
  "scan_semantics": "At scan k, inputs I[k] are sampled once, q[k] is pre-scan retained state, outputs O[k] are observed after execution, and q[k+1] is the updated state. Each test creates a fresh FB instance before step 0. An initialized instance has not yet executed a scan. Timer elapsed time is zero on the first eligible sampled invocation; dt_ms is elapsed wall time since the previous invocation, not automatically a synthetic input to the FB. No unobserved past input stability is assumed. All sequences here are expected values.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "Invalid range is diagnosed before invalid hysteresis width.",
    "No alarm update is allowed in an invalid-configuration scan."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Threshold comparisons are strict as written. Equality with trigger or release thresholds retains the previous alarm value.",
    "Invalid configuration returns early, preserving alarm outputs. error and status are recalculated each scan; valid configuration clears them.",
    "loLevel>=hiLevel takes priority over the hysteresis-width error. hystWindow is assumed nonnegative; negative values are outside the defined input domain.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "Floating-point inputs and intermediate reference arithmetic are finite. Existing fixed traces retain their declared absolute tolerance; claims do not extend to arbitrary magnitudes without a separately specified numeric error policy.",
    "All REAL inputs (value, loLevel, hiLevel, hystWindow) and reference threshold arithmetic (real32(hi-lo), real32(hi-width), real32(lo+width)) use IEEE 754 binary32 (REAL) rounding.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P1",
      "formula": "G(badRange -> (error & status=16#8001 & sameAlarms))",
      "explanation": "Invalid limits take priority and leave alarms unchanged.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P2",
      "formula": "G((!badRange & badWindow) -> (error & status=16#8002 & sameAlarms))",
      "explanation": "The hysteresis range must be smaller than the limit separation.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P3",
      "formula": "G(valid -> (!error & status=0))",
      "explanation": "Valid input clears transient configuration errors.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P4",
      "formula": "G((valid & Value>hiLevel) -> hiAlarm)",
      "explanation": "A high excursion activates the high alarm.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P5",
      "formula": "G((valid & Value<HighRelease) -> !hiAlarm)",
      "explanation": "Below the strict release boundary, high alarm clears.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P6",
      "formula": "G((valid & HighRelease<=Value & Value<=hiLevel) -> (hiAlarm=hiPrev))",
      "explanation": "The high hysteresis band retains history.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P7",
      "formula": "G((valid & Value<loLevel) -> loAlarm)",
      "explanation": "A low excursion activates the low alarm.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P8",
      "formula": "G((valid & Value>LowRelease) -> !loAlarm)",
      "explanation": "Above the strict low release boundary, low alarm clears.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB003.P9",
      "formula": "G((valid & loLevel<=Value & Value<=LowRelease) -> (loAlarm=loPrev))",
      "explanation": "The low hysteresis band retains history.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "badRange": "loLevel >= hiLevel",
    "badWindow": "real32(I.hystWindow)>=Span",
    "valid": "!badRange & !badWindow & hystWindow>=0",
    "hiPrev": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].hiAlarm\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].hiAlarm; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "loPrev": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].loAlarm\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].loAlarm; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "sameAlarms": "hiAlarm=hiPrev & loAlarm=loPrev",
    "interface names": "Identically named sampled input or observed output.",
    "Value": "I[k].Value: sampled input (REAL).",
    "hiLevel": "I[k].hiLevel: sampled input (REAL).",
    "loLevel": "I[k].loLevel: sampled input (REAL).",
    "hystWindow": "I[k].hystWindow: sampled input (REAL).",
    "hiAlarm": "O[k].hiAlarm: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "loAlarm": "O[k].loAlarm: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "error": "O[k].error: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "status": "O[k].status: independently observed post-scan candidate value (WORD); never defined as expected output.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.hiAlarm=false, O_init.loAlarm=false, O_init.error=false, O_init.status=0.",
    "HighRelease": "real32(real32(I.hiLevel)-real32(I.hystWindow))",
    "LowRelease": "real32(real32(I.loLevel)+real32(I.hystWindow))",
    "Span": "real32(real32(I.hiLevel)-real32(I.loLevel))",
    "real32": "IEEE754 binary32 rounding to nearest ties-to-even; finite declared domain. All REAL input symbols denote binary32 sampled values."
  }
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": [
    {
      "machine": "High alarm",
      "states": [
        "HI_OFF",
        "HI_ON"
      ],
      "initial_state": "HI_OFF",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "from": "HI_OFF",
          "to": "HI_ON",
          "guard": "valid AND Value > hiLevel"
        },
        {
          "from": "HI_ON",
          "to": "HI_OFF",
          "guard": "valid AND Value < real32(hiLevel - hystWindow)"
        },
        {
          "from": "HI_OFF",
          "to": "HI_OFF",
          "guard": "otherwise"
        },
        {
          "from": "HI_ON",
          "to": "HI_ON",
          "guard": "otherwise"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "machine": "Low alarm",
      "states": [
        "LO_OFF",
        "LO_ON"
      ],
      "initial_state": "LO_OFF",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "from": "LO_OFF",
          "to": "LO_ON",
          "guard": "valid AND Value < loLevel"
        },
        {
          "from": "LO_ON",
          "to": "LO_OFF",
          "guard": "valid AND Value > real32(loLevel + hystWindow)"
        },
        {
          "from": "LO_OFF",
          "to": "LO_OFF",
          "guard": "otherwise"
        },
        {
          "from": "LO_ON",
          "to": "LO_ON",
          "guard": "otherwise"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "timer_plan": [],
  "priorities": [
    "Evaluate loLevel >= hiLevel first: set error to TRUE and status to 16#8001.",
    "Otherwise, if hystWindow >= real32(hiLevel - loLevel), set error to TRUE and status to 16#8002.",
    "On either invalid configuration, preserve both alarm states. Skip alarm evaluation, but complete the timer and output stages.",
    "On valid configuration, clear error and status and evaluate the two alarm machines independently. Strict comparisons preserve the corresponding alarm at either hysteresis boundary.",
    "Assume nonnegative hystWindow and finite inputs and intermediate results. Use IEEE 754 binary32 rounding to nearest, ties to even, for the span and release thresholds; negative hystWindow is outside the defined domain."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "hiAlarm": false,
    "loAlarm": false,
    "error": false,
    "status": "16#0000",
    "qHi": false,
    "qLo": false,
    "diagError": false,
    "diagStatus": "16#0000",
    "inputs": "Externally supplied; no initial input values specified."
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    {
      "stage": 1,
      "name": "Edge sampling",
      "action": "Snapshot Value, hiLevel, loLevel and hystWindow once for the scan. No edge detectors are required."
    },
    {
      "stage": 2,
      "name": "Safety/reset priority and state transitions",
      "action": "Apply the configuration checks in priority order and set diagError and diagStatus every scan. On invalid configuration, retain qHi and qLo. Otherwise set diagError to FALSE and diagStatus to 16#0000, then update qHi and qLo independently using the state-machine transitions. There is no reset input."
    },
    {
      "stage": 3,
      "name": "Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF",
      "action": "No timer FBs are required; this stage contains no calls."
    },
    {
      "stage": 4,
      "name": "Unified output assignments",
      "action": "Assign hiAlarm := qHi, loAlarm := qLo, error := diagError, and status := diagStatus."
    }
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G((loLevel >= hiLevel) -> (error & status = 16#8001))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= real32(hiLevel - loLevel))) -> (error & status = 16#8002))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= 0.0) & (hystWindow < real32(hiLevel - loLevel))) -> (!error & status = 16#0000))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= 0.0) & (hystWindow < real32(hiLevel - loLevel)) & (Value > hiLevel)) -> hiAlarm)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= 0.0) & (hystWindow < real32(hiLevel - loLevel)) & (Value < real32(hiLevel - hystWindow))) -> !hiAlarm)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= 0.0) & (hystWindow < real32(hiLevel - loLevel)) & (Value < loLevel)) -> loAlarm)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "formula": "G(((loLevel < hiLevel) & (hystWindow >= 0.0) & (hystWindow < real32(hiLevel - loLevel)) & (Value > real32(loLevel + hystWindow))) -> !loAlarm)"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  }
]

